# Environment variables for the Vercel deployment target.
#
# This app currently requires NO env vars to build or run on Vercel — there
# are no secrets, no external API keys, and no server-only integrations.
# This file exists so future variables have a documented home; copy it to
# `.env.local` for local testing if you add any.
#
# Never commit a real `.env*` file — `.gitignore` already excludes them.

# --- Build metadata (optional, informational only) -------------------------
# On the Docker/server target, GIT_COMMIT_SHA and BUILD_TIME are baked in at
# `docker build` time and surfaced by GET /api/version. On Vercel, do NOT set
# these manually — Vercel injects its own equivalents automatically
# (VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, etc.), and app/api/version/route.ts already falls
# back to VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA when GIT_COMMIT_SHA is unset.

# --- If you add client-exposed config later ---------------------------------
# Anything the browser needs must be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ and is NOT a
# secret once set (it's inlined into the JS bundle at build time). Never put
# real secrets in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAMPLE=
